WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.751 --> 00:00:01.376
(Thunder)

00:00:01.376 --> 00:00:01.960
(Lightning)

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:03.795
Vera Farmiga:
Five Days At Memorial is a show

00:00:03.795 --> 00:00:05.339
about doctors and nurses

00:00:05.339 --> 00:00:07.549
Vera Farmiga:
in a hospital during Hurricane
Katrina.

00:00:07.549 --> 00:00:12.095
Vera Farmiga:
Who find themselves abandoned,
overwhelmed, and forced to make

00:00:12.095 --> 00:00:14.514
Vera Farmiga:
life and death choices under
extreme duress.

00:00:14.806 --> 00:00:17.559
We have this intense medical
ethics drama

00:00:17.559 --> 00:00:19.853
Carlton Cuse:
taking place during this huge
natural disaster,

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:23.857
Carlton Cuse:
and we wanted to be sure
we told both of those stories equally well.

00:00:23.982 --> 00:00:27.277
When we first started, we did 
rain outside the hospital. 

00:00:27.819 --> 00:00:33.408
Marcus Rait:
And so we have very large hoses
that come from a distribution tank in the parking lot.

00:00:33.575 --> 00:00:36.787
Marcus Rait:
And two "ten" power fans and two
"twenty" horsepower fans.

00:00:36.828 --> 00:00:41.833
Marcus Rait:
We put smoke behind the fans to
create that kind of haze of catastrophe.

00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:42.876
♪♪

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:45.545
And you could hear howling out
there, the wind machines. 

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:46.755
Julie Ann Emery:
 It sounded really eerie.

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:48.840
It's pretty loud, yeah.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:49.383
♪♪

00:00:49.383 --> 00:00:51.009
Marcus Rait:
It looks fantastic on the
inside.

00:00:51.134 --> 00:00:53.637
The walkway was one of these
incredible scenes.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:57.724
Marcus Rait:
The glass walkway gimbals, so it
creaks and shakes and glass breaks.

00:00:57.891 --> 00:01:01.770
It’s not done in post, it’s
actually very little left to the
imagination.

00:01:01.853 --> 00:01:03.730
Vera Farmiga:
There's some genuine fear, 
-(Laughs)

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:04.356
in those scenes.

00:01:04.398 --> 00:01:06.233
♪♪

00:01:06.233 --> 00:01:07.150
David Antonkiuk:
Action!

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:09.861
We have a massive outdoor pool.

00:01:10.195 --> 00:01:15.284
This tank holds approximately
four million liters of water,

00:01:15.617 --> 00:01:19.496
John Macgillivray:
and we've used a food
preservative and dyes to tint the water.

00:01:20.289 --> 00:01:22.374
Layton Morrison:
We’re gonna have police boats,
fan boats ,

00:01:22.374 --> 00:01:24.918
we’ll have people walking in the
water up to their chests.

00:01:25.127 --> 00:01:26.128
This is insane.

00:01:26.169 --> 00:01:29.631
It's gonna be a real experience
in a 4-4 1/2 foot pool.

00:01:29.798 --> 00:01:31.508
Layton Morrison:
Also we have a basement set.

00:01:31.675 --> 00:01:32.718
It's water coming!

00:01:32.718 --> 00:01:35.929
We had holding tanks on the
exterior of the building.

00:01:36.221 --> 00:01:39.224
Layton Morrison:
And we drop twelve-hundred
gallons of water on them in five seconds.

00:01:40.058 --> 00:01:41.268
Adepero Oduye:
You just have to say wow.

00:01:41.268 --> 00:01:42.769
I feel like I am there,

00:01:42.978 --> 00:01:44.855
Adepero Oduye:
at Memorial during Hurricane
Katrina.

00:01:45.022 --> 00:01:49.901
This is the most dedicated and
invested crew I have ever worked
with.

00:01:49.901 --> 00:01:53.572
I've never felt so supported by
a group.

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:57.743
♪♪

